cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Touchstone (Standard or library), please cite both the Standard and the library."
title: "Touchstone"
abstract: >
  Touchstone is a verification methodology and reference implementation
  for AI-coupled work whose scoring functions do not invoke an AI model
  on the output being measured. Standard 1.0 defines eleven measurement
  layers for output profiling (Section 5); Section 6 (Specification
  Compliance) is reserved for Standard 1.1. The library is the canonical
  reference implementation. v0.1 ships Section 5 measurement only, with
  two internal regression benchmarks: EXP-081 (12-document single-vendor
  corpus; Cohen's d=-5.238 tracking the recorded detector_v031 baseline
  of -5.43; 100% per-output gap-direction agreement; MAE 0.014 on
  unsourced rate) and EXP-095 (13 outputs, three model families;
  P-existence direction agreement 100%). Both benchmarks are
  project-authored regression baselines, not external replications;
  external-corpus validation is open work.
type: software
